    "text": "```python\ndef string_xor(a: str, b: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" Input are two strings a and b consisting only of 1s and 0s.\n    Perform binary string XOR on these inputs and return the result as a string.\n    >>> string_xor('010', '110')\n    '100'\n    \"\"\"\n    result = \"\"\n    \n    for bit_xor in zip_xor(a, b):\n        \n        result += ~bit_xor\n    \n    return result\n```\n\n\nThis function performs the XOR operation on the bits of the two input strings `a` and `b`, and returns the result as a string.\n\n\n\n```",
